Fixed-camera realistic side-view macro video with the full paper surface visible. At first a sheet of white watercolor paper is completely clean and blank with no blue mark. One large round blue ink droplet is clearly visible in the air above the paper, falls downward, and touches the center. Only after contact, a dark blue circular stain spreads outward and remains. | one large blue ink droplet | a dark blue circular stain spreads outward and remains
